# SECURITY-2D-3C1 — Docker build context = ./frontend. .gitignore does NOT apply to the build context, so
# `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile would otherwise ship whatever is on the build host's disk. This file keeps
# the context to the source `npm ci` + `npm run build` + `next start` actually need. Test SOURCES are kept
# (excluding only test ARTIFACTS) so `next build`'s TypeScript pass never breaks.

# VCS / OS noise
.git
.github
.DS_Store

# Secrets / keys — never in the image (the app reads NEXT_PUBLIC_* baked at build via the Docker build arg,
# and any server config from the process environment, not a copied .env).
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.crt

# Host dependencies + host build output — Docker rebuilds these itself (`npm ci` → node_modules,
# `npm run build` → .next). Copying the host copies would let a stale/foreign build shadow the clean one.
node_modules
.next
out
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test / cache / log ARTIFACTS (not test sources — those stay so the build's typecheck is complete).
coverage
.nyc_output
playwright-report
test-results
*.log
